{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"kind":"attribute","text":"@frozen"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"QueryRow"},{"kind":"text","text":"<each "},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"C"},{"kind":"text","text":">"}]}]},{"mentions":["doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/QueryingAWorld"],"kind":"mentions"},{"content":[{"type":"heading","anchor":"overview","level":2,"text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An update’s closure receives the components it writes as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"inout"},{"type":"text","text":" arguments and everything else"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it reads in a row. The row’s "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/QueryRow\/components","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" hold the read values in the order the update lists"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"them. An update that reads one type holds that type’s value itself, not a one-element tuple, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"an update that reads nothing holds "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"()"},{"type":"text","text":". An "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/AnyOf","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" term’s value is a tuple of optionals."}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["var world = World()","let comet = world.spawn(Position(x: 0, y: 0), Velocity(dx: 1, dy: 2), Health(current: 3))","","world.update(Position.self, reading: Velocity.self, Health.self) { position, row in","    let (velocity, health) = row.components","    position.x += velocity.dx * Double(health.current)","}","print(world[Position.self, of: comet])","\/\/ Prints \"Position(x: 3.0, y: 0.0)\""]}],"kind":"content"}],"s